_serialize_frontier: keep the leaves of each level as a set, journal the mutations

Sub-series: B (cycle search and frontier) - patch 4 of 6; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0003, 0006 only.

_serialize_tasks asks the frontier for the leaves of a priority level in
every pass of its selection loop. The frontier kept a heap of order-indices
per level with lazy deletion, so ready_nodes() drained and rebuilt the heap
on each call, and frontier_leaves() filtered the list again. Now every level
owns the exact set of its current leaves, updated in remove(), add_edge()
and _assign_index() at the points where a node's count of surviving children
reaches or leaves zero (the same test that validated a heap entry), and a
version counter that changes with the set. ready_nodes() sorts the set by
order-index, which is the order the heap produced. frontier_leaves() keeps
its last list per level and returns a copy while the level's version and
the size of scheduled_uninstalls (which only grows) are unchanged.
This patch also replaces the reduced form of patch 0006: its single
`mutations` counter becomes a journal (the list of removed nodes and the
number of add_edge calls). The no-cycle memo of 0006 keys on the two
journal sizes, which change exactly when `mutations` changed; the later
frontier patches read the same journal.

On top of patches 0001-0009, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 60.8 -> 59.9, holds 26.2 -> 25.9, masks 46.5 -> 47.2,
  py313 38.9 -> 38.0, bdeps 33.9 -> 34.1, policykit 26.2 -> 26.0
  sum of six 232.3 -> 231.1 (-1.2 s, -0.3 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0010 together: 447.5 -> 231.1 s (-48 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Kept as its own patch although its step is inside the noise: it is the
structural change (heaps to exact leaf sets, counter to journal) that
patches 0011 and 0024 build on, and it carries the replacement of the
reduced form of 0006.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* The leaf sets are exact only if every graph mutation goes through the
  frontier's remove()/add_edge(), which the counts already relied on. No
  lock-step comparison with the heap version was run.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
